## 4. PERFORMANCE / SMOOTHNESS PASS

Go through the app and apply these optimizations wherever applicable — this is a general pass, not a single bug fix, so check every screen/component listed:

### Lists and rendering
- On the Dashboard's document grid (`FlatList`), add: `removeClippedSubviews={true}`, a sensible `windowSize`, `maxToRenderPerBatch`, and `initialNumToRender` tuned for a 2-column grid, and `getItemLayout` if row heights are fixed/predictable (avoids expensive layout measurement).
- Wrap `DocumentCard` and other list-rendered components in `React.memo`, and make sure any inline arrow functions passed as `onPress` props to list items are wrapped in `useCallback` so list items don't re-render unnecessarily on every Dashboard re-render.

### Images
- Replace React Native's built-in `Image` component with `expo-image` (`npx expo install expo-image`) everywhere thumbnails/photos are displayed (Dashboard cards, Editor preview, PDF viewer, filter thumbnails) — it has built-in caching, better memory handling, and smoother loading/transition behavior than the core `Image` component.
- For document thumbnails specifically, generate and cache a small downscaled thumbnail (e.g. 200–300px wide) separately from the full-resolution page image, rather than rendering the full-size image scaled down at render time — this avoids decoding large images just to show a small grid thumbnail. Store the thumbnail path alongside the document's metadata.

### Heavy work off the interaction path
- Ensure image manipulation calls (`expo-image-manipulator` rotate/filter operations) and PDF generation (`expo-print`) don't block UI feedback — confirm loading states are shown immediately (before the heavy async call starts) rather than only after, so taps feel instantly acknowledged even while processing continues.
- Where reasonable, wrap non-urgent post-navigation work (like kicking off the next interstitial preload, or refreshing storage-usage stats on the Dashboard) in `InteractionManager.runAfterInteractions()` so it doesn't compete with an in-progress screen transition animation for the JS thread.

### General React hygiene
- Audit for unnecessary re-renders: any context (`useScanSession`, ad consent state, etc.) that changes frequently should be scoped tightly so it doesn't force unrelated components to re-render. Split contexts if one large context is causing broad re-renders from small, frequent updates.
- Memoize expensive derived values (e.g., formatted file sizes/dates on the Dashboard list, filtered/sorted document lists) with `useMemo` instead of recomputing on every render.

### Native/build-level
- Confirm the New Architecture (Fabric/TurboModules) is enabled if the installed Expo SDK/RN version supports it well for all currently-used native modules (check for any known incompatibilities with `expo-camera`, `expo-print`, or `react-native-google-mobile-ads` first — don't enable it if it would break camera or ads functionality; if uncertain, leave it as-is and note that decision rather than guessing).
- Confirm Hermes is the JS engine (default in modern Expo, but verify it wasn't accidentally overridden).

